{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031075-antinomian-magic-dealing-with-the-abyss","id":1031075,"title":"Antinomian Magic = 'Dealing with the Abyss'?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-13T03:58:42-08:00","id":1031075,"title":"Antinomian Magic = 'Dealing with the Abyss'?","content":"Does inviting Paradox into your spell as a Scelesti count as the Falling-level Act of Hubris 'dealing with the Abyss', or is that meant for even more severe acts, such as negotiating with the Old Man, etc?<br /> <br /> It seems strange that a Scelesti could become one of the Mad after casting 7 spells, assuming they were of average Wisdom when they became Scelesti (doubtful)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T04:05:40-08:00","id":1031079,"title":"","content":"1E Rules:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Soul-Shaking: Casting an antinomian spell forces an immediate degeneration check for mages with Wisdom 3 or more (roll 2 dice). </div> </div> </div> Seems like a good place to put this would be that it's a sin for Understanding Level, but not Falling, which avoids the whole instant Scelesti-&gt;Mad fast track.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T05:06:41-08:00","id":1031092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031075-antinomian-magic-dealing-with-the-abyss#post1031075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems strange that a Scelesti could become one of the Mad after casting 7 spells, assuming they were of average Wisdom when they became Scelesti (doubtful)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if that was the author intent, but I could see an argument for it.<br /> <br /> You're basically just opening yourself up to the Abyss in a fairly uncontrolled manner; the use of legacies and Abyssal watchtowers at least somewhat mediates the madness. Being a successful Scelesti means managing your own degeneration, and clearly a lot of them do fail and go Mad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T05:49:00-08:00","id":1031108,"title":"","content":"Just because you can invite Abyss to your spells doesn't mean you should invite it to all the spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T06:01:41-08:00","id":1031110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031075-antinomian-magic-dealing-with-the-abyss?p=1031108#post1031108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because you can invite Abyss to your spells doesn't mean you should invite it to all the spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true, I think the number you can add it to before being rendered Mad is probably intended to be higher than 7-10.<br /> Especially since in 1E, you couldn't drop below Wisdom 2 from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T06:03:43-08:00","id":1031112,"title":"","content":"Maybe, depending on the level of Scelesti initiation (I recall there are 3 'degrees' of Scelesti), you're &quot;inured&quot; to inviting paradox, meaning it's never a Hubris act to do this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T06:19:11-08:00","id":1031117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031075-antinomian-magic-dealing-with-the-abyss?p=1031110#post1031110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially since in 1E, you couldn't drop below Wisdom 2 from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but the system worked differently. You could only go Mad from the very worst atrocities or stealing someones soul. 2e folds in a few of the higher sins into Falling. The 1e core had casual murder as a Wisdom 2 sin and that would seem to come under Falling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T06:26:37-08:00","id":1031119,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't inuring yourself to a spell make this irrelevant? I don't remember the wording, but didn't inure made you flat out never lose wisdom from a Spell X?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T06:27:47-08:00","id":1031120,"title":"","content":"Also, Act of Hubris is not automatic dropping of Wisdom - there are also 'STs factors' and using AoH on Virtue of your character, both can give you +1 bonus to roll, making dicepools 2-3 - and by this 'rather should pass' kind a roll. I <i>really</i> think that most Scelesti see their usage of Abyssal magic as 'necessary' by their Virtue or other 'redeeming factors'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T06:33:02-08:00","id":1031121,"title":"","content":"Wisdom is about thinking things through and just like with murder you could possibly lift dealing with Abyss from Falling to Understanding if you know what your doing and what are the consequences of your actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T06:38:23-08:00","id":1031124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031075-antinomian-magic-dealing-with-the-abyss?p=1031119#post1031119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't inuring yourself to a spell make this irrelevant? I don't remember the wording, but didn't inure made you flat out never lose wisdom from a Spell X?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, but, like I said, it might depend on how much you're in deep with the whole Scelestus thing. If you're an occasional user of antinomian magic, well, you should be losing wisdom. Otoh, if you're serious about becoming a full-blown abyssal mage, you're likely joining a Scelestus legacy and going through all three stages, getting your own abyssal Ziggurat. By then, I believe that dabbling in antinomian magic won't affect your wisdom anymore. [Not that I believe it'll be any higher than, say, 3].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T06:55:38-08:00","id":1031131,"title":"","content":"Good insights, all. Some of those extra factors are worth considering, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T07:23:05-08:00","id":1031146,"title":"","content":"What I meant is:<br /> <br /> You like to cast Fireball. You Fireballed a baddie. You also Fireballed a kitten. This made you lose a Wisdom point. You decided to say &quot;Fireballs before kittens&quot; and Inured yourself to Fireballing. No matter what you do, Fireball won't provoke Wisdom loses. Fireball 100000 kittens? No Wisdom loss. <br /> This would mean that if you want to keep healthy Wisdom as a Scelestus, you need to pick some favorite, signature spells and stick to them when it comes to abyss-ing. Which is good. Anything that makes create spellcasting patterns and make them focus on a few options at a time is good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T14:00:22-08:00","id":1031318,"title":"","content":"You could always decide that, after a certain level of exposure, the Scelestus has habituated to the toll such magic places upon their soul. The Acts of Hubris list is, after all, meant to be adaptable and, indeed, I would say that even for the same character, the same act may not be an Act of Hubris forever. The Mage's soul becomes scarred; the wounds no longer cut as deep. Eventually, those acts of evil push you to a place where you sit comfortably.<br /> <br /> Even if the Mage core only divides morality into three categories, you don't have to. You can still distinguish between 4 and 5 dots on the moral scale and use the sections as guidelines for the sort of Mage that would be in them.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, I have an urge to monkey with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T14:04:56-08:00","id":1031321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031075-antinomian-magic-dealing-with-the-abyss?p=1031318#post1031318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could always decide that, after a certain level of exposure, the Scelestus has habituated to the toll such magic places upon their soul. The Acts of Hubris list is, after all, meant to be adaptable and, indeed, I would say that even for the same character, the same act may not be an Act of Hubris forever. The Mage's soul becomes scarred; the wounds no longer cut as deep. Eventually, those acts of evil push you to a place where you sit comfortably.<br /> <br /> Even if the Mage core only divides morality into three categories, you don't have to. You can still distinguish between 4 and 5 dots on the moral scale and use the sections as guidelines for the sort of Mage that would be in them.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, I have an urge to monkey with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be interested in the results if you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T15:43:09-08:00","id":1031357,"title":"","content":"It's something I've tried to work with before and the subjective nature of it makes it somewhat difficult. Wisdom is one of the harder stats to adjudicate, because while it is ostensibly about thinking through the consequences of one's actions, there isn't really a particularly efficacious point to say the Mage wasn't thinking through the consequences. After all, a Mage who kills in a panic is putting as much thought into their actions as one who realizes they forgot their spouse's anniversary and hastily races to get some flowers. Both ended up in a situation they really wish they hadn't been in, and might not have been in if they'd put more thought and care into it, but something tells me that Golden Eyes slashing her trusted Sleepwalker friend's throat because no-one could be allowed to know she accidentally caused an Abyssal manifestation is going to call for a Wisdom roll at the Falling level, while Drake apologizes, gives the gift, offers a dinner out to make up for it, and either gets off with a night or two of annoyance or, if he's charming, some slow and romantic make-up sex. He might have to be on his good behaviour but his soul doesn't degrade.<br /> <br /> The thing is, both actions have consequences that will echo on into eternity. All actions do. So why is one that results in death and pain and misery judged harshly? Likewise, what if a Mage, through carelessness and bravado, accidentally uncovers a new healing rote that is somehow better than all previous ones and lets them help tons of sick people, with no strings attached?<br /> <br /> I do not subscribe to moral luck. If Wisdom is a measure of short-sightedness, it should always be such, regardless of whether the consequences are good or bad.<br /> <br /> As a corollary to this point, I would point to Vampire, wherein a Vampire will <i>still</i> face a Humanity roll if they leap to the rescue of a family trapped in a sinking car, using their lack of a need for oxygen and superhuman strength to save the day. They'll get a bonus to the roll, because they acted out of compassion for other human beings and at personal risk (the Masquerade would be violated hard), but the roll still has to be made.<br /> <br /> Wisdom needs to find an anchor for itself. Since scale of consequence is sort of bollocks for it (after all, everything is going to have an uncountably large number of consequences on a long enough time scale), all that is left to do is find something else to hang it on; some better core to build around.<br /> <br /> So... That's what I'm going to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T15:56:01-08:00","id":1031363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031075-antinomian-magic-dealing-with-the-abyss#post1031075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does inviting Paradox into your spell as a Scelesti count as the Falling-level Act of Hubris 'dealing with the Abyss', or is that meant for even more severe acts, such as negotiating with the Old Man, etc?<br /> <br /> It seems strange that a Scelesti could become one of the Mad after casting 7 spells, assuming they were of average Wisdom when they became Scelesti (doubtful)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is what the inuring mechanic is for. &quot;This act no longer forces Wisdom rolls, but risks Paradox every time I do it&quot; is <i>entirely</i> appropriate for a Scelestus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T21:36:11-08:00","id":1031446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031075-antinomian-magic-dealing-with-the-abyss?p=1031363#post1031363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is what the inuring mechanic is for. &amp;quot;This act no longer forces Wisdom rolls, but risks Paradox every time I do it&amp;quot; is <i>entirely</i> appropriate for a Scelestus.</div> </div> </div> </div>If only you could inure against a specific sin and not just 1 spell per gnosis. Kind of like of VtR does banes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[